# Cloudflare Pages response headers — security baseline for the public-body site.
# adapter-cloudflare copies this root _headers file verbatim into .svelte-kit/cloudflare.
#
# NOTE: Content-Security-Policy is NOT set here. SvelteKit's hydration bootstrap
# is an inline <script> whose sha256 hash changes every build, so a static
# header policy with script-src 'self' would block it (it did — broke the mobile
# nav drawer). The CSP is managed by kit.csp in svelte.config.js (hash/nonce
# mode). Framing protection stays here via X-Frame-Options: DENY, because
# frame-ancestors is ignored in <meta>-delivered CSP.
#
# There is deliberately NO path-scoped block for /admin. The panel is SvelteKit
# routes rather than a static single-page app, so it is covered by the same
# kit.csp policy as every other route. Do not re-introduce a path-scoped block
# and do not widen kit.csp to accommodate the panel.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()
